2. The Third Arena / Naught Protocol

Context

If one participant chooses the language, definitions, evidence rules, tempo, and victory condition, then the contest measures adaptation to that participant’s machinery rather than truth.

Naught is the zeroing operation: neither frame begins as sovereign.

Minimal common ground

• Neither participant owns truth.
• Claims must produce consequences or discriminations.
• Terms and victory conditions may be challenged.
• The person survives the argument.
• Reality receives the final vote.

Contest covenant

> Maximum pressure on the claim; minimum unnecessary damage to the claimant.

The Rocky / Drago mode is vigorous allied contest:

• attack claims, not human worth;
• no cheap shots or deliberate destabilization;
• no importing literal violence into an intellectual arena;
• either participant may call the bell when pressure ceases to produce growth;
• the goal is not personal supremacy, but a stronger survivor-model.

Failure mode

Pure naught cannot host a contest. With no shared invariants, every losing move can reject the arena. The Third Arena therefore begins at zero but must construct provisional rules that remain open to revision by deltas.

