7. Wolf at night: fear integrated into orientation

The wolf’s advantage is not the absence of fear. It is a sensory and relational architecture that turns threat information into orientation.

```text
sample air → listen → locate pack → recall terrain → update distance → move
```

Night is not an empty unknown; it is an environment the wolf’s senses are prepared to interpret.

> Courage does not erase threat perception. It prevents threat perception from owning the steering wheel.

An animal convinced it has nothing to fear is not necessarily apex; it may be the next carcass.

