8. Language as recursive leverage—and its pyramid failure mode

Every elevated word recruits older words, sensations, memories, distinctions, and embodied experiences beneath it. A small token can command an enormous downline of accumulated meaning.

Language is normally a recursive leverage network, not literally a pyramid scheme, because value can flow both upward and downward and additional participants can enrich the network.

Pyramid failure mode: authority laundering through abstraction

1. Coin an elevated term.
2. Define it using other elevated terms.
3. Let institutions repeat it.
4. Treat repetition as evidence.
5. Demand allegiance without redeeming the symbol into observable reality.

Semantic solvency audit

Ask every important term to cash itself out into one or more of:

• discriminations;
• predictions;
• experiences;
• operations;
• actions;
• falsifiers.

If redemption is continually deferred to another symbol, the semantic bank may be insolvent.

