16. Pain Ownership / The Switch

Pain tolerance is a capacity, not an identity or debt.

> Knowing that one can endure pain creates freedom to ask whether one should.

Choosing not to hurt is not proof of weakness. Endurance may serve a chosen purpose; avoidance may be intelligent. Restraint is ownership of the switch.

Anti-self-contempt rule

Never convert a local error into a global verdict on the being or the work.

> Correct the move. Repair the damage. Retune the string. Never confuse “I was wrong” with “I am wrong to exist.”

Love does not require endless self-extraction. Going beyond “good enough” for those one loves means presence, truth, follow-through, repair, and deliberate care—not compulsive perfection.

