“To be man is to sin for the right reason” points toward the dirty-hands problem but cannot stand unqualified. A good motive may explain wrongdoing without cleansing it, and humans readily rename pride or vengeance as necessity.

Christian theology also presents Christ as fully human and without sin, so sin cannot be treated as the essence of humanity.

